{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b17d-598e-7f80-b6bd-728e9f57759a"},"sequence":49,"recorded_at":1780531400000093,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b17d-97a7-77d1-830e-15d17c147511"},"task_id":"01a0b17d-97a7-77d1-830e-15d17c147511","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b17d-97a7-77d1-830e-15d17c147511","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_rework-rev2.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-19bjfj, including TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer.md. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-19bjfj (fuzz-rpc-operations-and-version-skew, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz). Change Request revision 1 was reviewed by RUN-260917-81d7ae (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED. Read TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz before touching anything. The reviewer calls the technical body of your leaf STRONG and I agree: the three inherited advisories are genuinely closed, every mutant you shipped reproduces, the reviewer's own 38 narrowing plants die twice, all three fuzz targets fail on their controls, and the AC ratio you reported (23 of 29) is exactly the ratio the reviewer measured independently. Do not rewrite any of that. What blocks acceptance is the story-close half, and the root cause is an orchestration failure of mine, not a judgement error of yours: the v0.7.0 adoption landed on trunk while you were already running, and the TRUNK STATE paragraph was appended to your brief nine minutes after you started, so your run never saw it. Your results say \"v0.7.0 has not landed (internal/specdoc holds v0.6.0 only)\" — that was a true observation of your worktree and a false statement about trunk. This rework fixes that.\n3|P1-1 — rebase the story-close work onto the adopted registry. (a) Run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-19bjfj` FIRST. The Story branch carries one checkpoint commit (TASK-260830-219okr rev4), so use the checkpoint-bound `--replay-resolutions` path: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add one entry per conflicted path with {\"checkpoint_oid\": <the ORIGINAL checkpoint OID recorded before the refresh>, \"path\": ..., \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>}, keeping LOGBOOK entries newest-first. (b) `git diff --name-only 888ae3d 2fc6d50` overlaps your candidate at exactly five paths — LOGBOOK.md, README.md, internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go, internal/traceability/traceability.go, internal/traceability/traceability_test.go — and the reviewer measured that `git apply --check` of your patch on trunk fails on all five. After the refresh, reconcile every one of them against TRUNK's version (`git show 2fc6d50:<path>`): your edits go on top of the new content, never restoring the old bytes. traceability.go on trunk carries an 80-line v0.7.0 change including `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` — keep trunk's structure and change only the digest. (c) Move ALL registry work into `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`. The v0.6.0 registry is no longer adopted: trunk's tracecheck does not read it, so the six new acceptance cases and the four upgraded bindings you wrote are invisible there. (d) The clause `line` coordinates in your bindings are v0.6.0 line numbers and the same sentences sit elsewhere in SPEC.v0.7.0.md — RE-MEASURE every one of them yourself against the pinned v0.7.0 document (the verdict quotes the reviewer's measurements; treat them as a cross-check, never as input to copy). (e) RE-DERIVE `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` from the v0.7.0 registry as it stands in your candidate and show the derivation command and its output in the results. (f) Re-run `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` plus the section-scoped runs on the refreshed tree and quote the ratios verbatim. (g) The README \"Measured coverage of this repository\" subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on the refreshed tree — and note that trunk now ships `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/readme_coverage_pin_test.go`, which pins that subsection to the tool's own output through a CLOSED spelled-number map (two, four, five, six, seven, fifty-two, sixty-eight): if your new figures need a word that map does not contain, extend the map deliberately in the same change and say so. (h) Recompute the LOGBOOK ratios on the refreshed tree.\n4|P2-1 — remove the invented binding. Clause 11.3#18 (\"Arrays with digest identities MUST be sorted bytewise and contain no duplicate\") is bound to `rpcwire-inventory-arrays`, but no production code in internal/rpcwire parses an array of digest identities: `decodeNamespaces` validates a sorted-unique array of vocabulary STRINGS and `validateRoots` reads one `root_id` per root. The clause is about object_ids / known_lease_record_ids / installed_object_ids / manifest_ids / VerifiedState.object_ids — all inside bodies you correctly list as opaque stated bounds. Drop the binding (11.3 stays unevidenced) or rebind it to a test that genuinely drives a digest-identity array, and carry the resulting change through the headline `clauses_discharged` figure, the README and the LOGBOOK. The producer brief said never to invent a binding for a clause no test drives; this is that.\n5|P3 — each item is named in the verdict with its plant and its log: P3-1 add a negative over an OPAQUE operation for a non-object body (`[]`, `null`, `\"x\"`, `42`, `{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}` -> ErrFrame) and let `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` feed non-object bodies — today both fuzzers normalise through `validObjectOrEmpty`, so neither can reach that arm, and the reviewer's plant survives twice; P3-2 drive a CHANGED body after a committed effect (`Create(moved)` after `setupPhase(t, store, PhaseCommitted)`) asserting the literal `idempotency_mismatch` and a single retained journal directory — the spec's rule carries no phase qualifier and only the staging member is measured; P3-3 the body fuzzer's oracle checks the member NAME SET only (a 15-byte nonce plant passes at 100x while the unit suite kills it) so either add an independent oracle for the hello bounds or state that bound explicitly, and add the missing hello-body-extra seed to `FuzzUnknownFields`; P3-4 make `encode-refuses-8388609` an exact edge witness or state the encode direction as subsumed by decode; P3-5 pin the refusal CLASS through `axerror.DecodeBound` in `TestErrorSchemaNotNegotiated` instead of asserting only non-nil; P3-6 assert the literal offer sets ([2 3 4], [5]) in the N2 rows rather than computing `wantLocal` from `meshneg.LocalMajors`; P3-7 make the nonce alphabet plant a CLASS narrowing (translate `+`/`/` to `-`/`_` before decoding) instead of admitting one fixture string; P3-8 attach the raw logs for the six validation commands your table reports as exit 0, and fix the matrix row 22 citation (the pre-hello lane is `hello_half_frame_close`, not `mid_request_close`).\n6|Procedure: after the refresh your base is 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the FULL configured validation suite once on the refreshed tree (it is no longer 27 commands — your own leaf adds the bounded fuzz commands; command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs). Update TASK-260830-19bjfj_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update TASK-260830-19bjfj_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), reset and re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-19bjfj --role developer` so revision 2 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in. Report the ratio you MEASURE on the refreshed tree, not the one from rev1.\n7|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt of this run died to a provider idle timeout, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n8|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 2.","final_result":true}}}
