{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8cd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b17d-598e-7f80-b6bd-728e9f57759a"},"sequence":705,"recorded_at":1780531400001405,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b181-64fe-7c81-85bc-ceb1c83518d3"},"task_id":"01a0b181-64fe-7c81-85bc-ceb1c83518d3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b181-64fe-7c81-85bc-ceb1c83518d3","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-25-1\",\n  \"command\": \"diff /tmp/lb_base.md /tmp/rev1/LOGBOOK.md | head -40; echo ===; head -30 /tmp/rev1/LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"View rev1 LOGBOOK entry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"4a5,15\\n> \\n> ## 2026-09-18\\n> \\n> ### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj: adversarial closure\\n> - DELIVERED (test-only; no production behavior file changed): `internal/rpcwire/adversarial_test.go` (closed-body member/bound sweeps for the two parsed bodies, per-member namespace vocabulary + 30-cell mismatch matrix, unknown-field sweep over every closed shape, both §17.1 extension directions, correlation classes, major-1 rejection, error-schema-not-negotiated, framing bounds) and `internal/rpcwire/fuzz_adversarial_test.go` (FuzzClosedOperationBodies over the 24-op vocabulary, FuzzNamespaceVocabulary with a spec-transcribed oracle, FuzzUnknownFields over raw lines — each with a planted control that FAILS, then removed); `internal/meshneg/adversarial_test.go` (N1 per-key sweep for every frame/key through Negotiate, N2 Local-fact pins, six no-coercion shapes + major-1 through the composed entry) plus the N3 `refuse-local-names-1` row. Registered the 3 fuzz targets as bounded validation commands (task-board.config.json +3 rows, stated explicitly).\\n> - N1-N3 (inherited P3s, all closed): membership sweep kills per-key exemption plants at every key (reviewer's S7/S8/S9 class); Local==LocalMajors(generation) asserted on all shape+mixed rows (kills S12); local-1 row placed beside a common major after the first revision proved unobservable (disjoint refusal subsumes the plant — the harness caught it, fixed before the evidence run). Reachability bound stated: LocalMajors never yields 1.\\n> - MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 40 killed / neutral passed / new error-text SURVIVED control (exit 0). One honest sentinel-swap row (correlation-id-maps-frame) labeled as swap, not narrowing; one token-preserving narrowing (`namespace-admits-six-letter`, pinned tokens still match exactly). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n> - TRACEABILITY: upgraded 4 unevidenced bindings (11.2 partial 3/5, 11.3 sliver 1/27, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4) with 6 new acceptance cases incl. story case `story-4qojoz-mesh-negotiation` over the real conformance suite; prior owners' cases merged, none orphaned; 17.2/17.3 keep existing unevidenced owners. Digest re-derived `1500e259…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `57/535` (+8); section-scoped runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate table updates in traceability_test.go/main_test.go + README figures/paragraph (138 cases).\\n> - BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque (no initiator/lease revalidation entry exists); no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id is correlation-only (no responder replay cache — replay/idempotency evidence adopted from matjournal `TestCreateReplayAndConflict`/crash suite plus new `TestRPCBlindRetryAfterCommitNeverDoubles`); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n> - PROCESS: a fuzzer \\\"finding\\\" on first smoke was an oracle bug (JSON replaces invalid UTF-8; guarded with utf8.ValidString). Fuzz controls must use `-fuzztime=100x`: `10x` caps TOTAL execs including seeds, so late seeds never run (control falsely passed until rerun). A stray shell `>` typo truncated `internal/matjournal/journal_test.go` mid-session; restored byte-identical from the checkpoint (`git checkout --`, verified via clean status); no evidence depends on the incident window.\\n> - Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n7a19,27\\n> ### TASK-260830-219okr — dual-stack major negotiation (first leaf)\\n> - DELIVERED: `internal/meshneg` (`Negotiate`/`LocalMajors`/`PeerOffer`/`Select` over `Refusal`/`Decision` pure data): generation-to-majors mapping (Config-1: 2; Config-2: 2,3; Config-3: 2,3,4; Config-4: exactly 5), single-major peer-offer validation against the framing major, highest-common selection, no-common-major refusal with registry-resolved `incompatible_protocol`/6 (unknown config: `invalid_config`/3), exact per-major contracts/namespaces/bound error versions rebuilt from rpcwire/axerror, and core-only peer exposure (`directory_mesh_unsupported`, `terminal_backend_unavailable`), never zero inventory. Frames nothing, admits nothing, pure/stateless. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n> - BINDING CHOICE: the RPC-4 exposure equivalent is the registered `terminal_backend_unavailable` (exit 6), not a minted token — Section 11.9 requires reporting evidence unsupported rather than empty and 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable; the 1.3.0 exit-6 row carries exactly that code. Refusal/exposure exits resolve via `axerror.ExitCodeFor` under each code's introducing version; cross-version stability is asserted by test, not assumed.\\n> - MUTANTS: 27 narrowing probes killed by named tests (neutral passed, harmless Detail-text control SURVIVED as designed; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`). Two initial SURVIVEDs were test gaps the harness caught: substituted-keys (same count, caught by membership loop, not length check) and peer-mixing-1-beside-common (unobservable without overlap) — both closed with new cases before the evidence run. Successor run RUN-260917-244f06 re-executed the harness: 27 killed, neutral passed, control SURVIVED (exit 0), and corrected the earlier \\\"28\\\" count.\\n> - BOUNDS: v2 1-16 minor ranges select the major only (within-major minor selection future work); handshake sequencing stays with rpcwire decode + the responder; admission (identity/allowlist/generation) stays with TASK-260830-z1yxg9 with separation pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`; no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claimed. Traceability registry/digest untouched for the story final leaf (package-local TRACEABILITY.md only).\\n> - AC: 11 of 11 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n> - REV3 (RUN-260917-27bea1): rev1/rev2 CR validation both failed at suite command 5/27 on the sessquery race-timeout (default 10m, load-dependent, leaf-independent); trunk `888ae3d` fixed it systemically with an explicit `-timeout 25m`. Refreshed the candidate onto `888ae3d` (`refresh_advanced`, config restored to HEAD by hand, production untouched) and ran the full 27-command suite once: all exits 0, race gate 38 ok with sessquery 515.663s and no DATA RACE, meshneg 87.8%, mutants 27 killed / neutral passed / control SURVIVED.\\n> - REV4 (RUN-260917-8fb798): rev3 review (RUN-260917-92b548) routed CHANGES REQUESTED with 3xP2 + 3xP3, all evidence/docs, production selection logic accepted unchanged. F1: exposure expectations now assert the literal `directory_mesh_unsupported` / `terminal_backend_unavailable` tokens at the Negotiate entry (no committed test derives from the production constants) + 2 same-exit swap plants. F2: new `TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration` drives unknown generations x every frame through Negotiate (invalid_config/3, zero Decision) + Negotiate-site fallback plant. F3: docs name `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` (not the normalized SchemaVersion) + `TestLocalMajorsTracksConfigVocabulary` pins the mapping against config.Version1/Version2/CurrentVersion/Version4 with a Decode-level normalization proof. F4: stated bound (non-rpc arrays validated by rpcwire decode, trusted here; direct callers must pass decode-produced hellos) pinned by `TestPeerOfferTrustsDecodedNonRPCArrays`; probe showed v2 lease 9.9.9 is admitted by decode too (valid range by design, not a hole). F5: frame rows 4.1.0/5.0.1/5.1.0 + 5.x-edge plant + unparseable-class bound stated. F6: TRACEABILITY 17.1 minor clause dropped. Harness now 31 narrowing killed / neutral passed / control SURVIVED (exit 0); 18/18 package tests green; full 27-command suite green (38 ok verbose/race/cover, race sessquery 370.955s no DATA RACE, meshneg 87.8%).\\n> \\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj: adversarial closure\\n- DELIVERED (test-only; no production behavior file changed): `internal/rpcwire/adversarial_test.go` (closed-body member/bound sweeps for the two parsed bodies, per-member namespace vocabulary + 30-cell mismatch matrix, unknown-field sweep over every closed shape, both §17.1 extension directions, correlation classes, major-1 rejection, error-schema-not-negotiated, framing bounds) and `internal/rpcwire/fuzz_adversarial_test.go` (FuzzClosedOperationBodies over the 24-op vocabulary, FuzzNamespaceVocabulary with a spec-transcribed oracle, FuzzUnknownFields over raw lines — each wi