se returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.2. TASK-260830-z1yxg9 adds rpcwire.DecodeRequest/DecodeResponse structural envelopes, request-ID/version correlation, 14-key hello maps, nonce echo and limit floors for RPC 2/3/4/5, and the hostchannel Serve/Dial authenticated hello consumer with its refusal table (internal/hostchannel, HC-HELLO/HC-DISPATCH families). No clause of 11.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 5 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n}\\n--- NEW:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:11.2\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/rpcwire/envelope.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"DecodeRequest\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"rpcwire-closed-bodies\\\",\\n  \\\"rpcwire-framing\\\",\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"11.2#2\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 7179,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"state, Structured Error, Observation Event, and CLI Result MUST NOT appear in\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"rpcwire-closed-bodies\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"11.2#3\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 7223,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"<code>ok = false</code> and one Structured Error and MUST omit body. Unknown\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"rpcwire-framing\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"11.2#4\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 7235,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"at least the values shown and MUST refuse a peer below them. The 5 MiB object\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"rpcwire-closed-bodies\\\"\\n   ]\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.2 clauses 11.2#1 and 11.2#5 (hello-first sequencing) are executed only for the RPC-5 Host Channel responder: DecodeRequest is a stateless codec with no handshake memory, and no legacy `ax rpc serve` responder exists in the tree, so the legacy sequencing lane stays a stated bound while the codec-enforced clauses discharge above.\\\"\\n}\\n================================================================================\\nCHANGED: section:11.3\\n--- OLD:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:11.3\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3. rpcwire now validates inventory.roots namespace/cardinality (6/7/8/8 across RPC 2/3/4/5) and matches roots to requested namespaces, and hostchannel dispatches authorized post-hello inventory.roots calls through the current-generation gate (TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel). No Merkle digest verification, schema membership or object exchange exists. No clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n}\\n--- NEW:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:11.3\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/rpcwire/envelope.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"EncodeSuccess\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"rpcwire-inventory-arrays\\\",\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"sliver\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"11.3#18\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 7549,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"Arrays with digest identities MUST be sorted bytewise and contain no duplicate.\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"rpcwire-inventory-arrays\\\"\\n   ]\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.3 carries 27 normative clauses and only 11.3#18 (sorted-unique digest arrays, inventory.roots lanes) is driven through EncodeSuccess: every other operation body is opaque to this story's codec (22 unparsed operations are stated bounds), mutation and fencing-token revalidation belong to the fencing and hosttrust owners, and materialization journal, bridge, and progress clauses belong to the matjournal and provhost owners. No Merkle digest verification, schema membership or object exchange exists.\\\"\\n}\\n================================================================================\\nCHANGED: section:17.1\\n--- OLD:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:17.1\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/config/schema.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Decode\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"config-versioned-readers\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Decode reads every pinned Section 17.1 document version, but no clause of Section 17.1 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\n}\\n--- NEW:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:17.1\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/meshneg/negotiate.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Negotiate\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"meshneg-selection\\\",\\n  \\\"rpcwire-version-boundary\\\",\\n  \\\"config-versioned-readers\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"17.1#1\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 15146,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"- a major increment MAY break syntax or semantics and MUST require explicit\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"meshneg-selection\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"17.1#4\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 15168,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"highest mutually supported minor within a common major; they MUST NOT select a\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"meshneg-selection\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"17.1#5\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 15181,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"immutable v0.1.0 contracts and MUST NOT be interpreted using the corrected\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"meshneg-selection\\\",\\n    \\\"rpcwire-version-boundary\\\"\\n   ]\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 17.1 clauses 17.1#2 (minor-version semantic preservation) and 17.1#6 (v1 materialization upgrade) are outside Negotiate, which selects majors only: no minor-selection entry exists, immutable-object namespaced extensions (17.1#3) belong to the object-exchange owners, and materialization upgrade belongs to the matjournal and provhost owners. The retained config-versioned-readers case keeps the config Decode lanes traceable.\\\"\\n}\\n================================================================================\\nCHANGED: section:17.4\\n--- OLD:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:17.4\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/config/migration.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"AssessCompatibility\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"config-read-only-downgrade\\\",\\n  \\\"config-durable-migration\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"AssessCompatibility implements the Section 17.4 read-only downgrade assessment, but no clause of Section 17.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\n}\\n--- NEW:\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:17.4\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/meshneg/negotiate.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Negotiate\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"story-4qojoz-mesh-negotiation\\\",\\n  \\\"config-read-only-downgrade\\\",\\n  \\\"config-durable-migration\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"sliver\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"17.4#4\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 15240,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"immutable evidence; it MUST report activation unavailable rather than omit the\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"story-4qojoz-mesh-negotiation\\\"\\n   ]\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 17.4 clauses 17.4#1 through 17.4#3 (upgrade checks, downgraded-binary read-only mode, no resume or transfer) are outside Negotiate: no upgrade, downgrade, or auto-resume flow exists in the tree, so only the activation-unavailable exposure clause discharges above. The retained config cases keep the AssessCompatibility downgrade-assessment lanes traceable.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7392,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1848,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
