{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca77","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b17d-598e-7f80-b6bd-728e9f57759a"},"sequence":918,"recorded_at":1780531400001831,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ee667c6e-43c2-4b33-805c-7f4df74b7dba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b182-3c8a-7881-b12d-d09419314174"},"task_id":"01a0b182-3c8a-7881-b12d-d09419314174","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b182-3c8a-7881-b12d-d09419314174","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-34-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n -i \\\"clause\\\\|excerpt\\\\|orphan\\\\|unreferenced\\\" internal/traceability/traceability.go | head -50; echo ===; wc -l internal/traceability/traceability.go\",\n  \"description\": \"Find clause verification logic\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"59:\\t// the registered section bindings, not a prose claim. NormativeClauses is\\n60:\\t// the number of RFC 2119 clause lines the pinned document itself carries in\\n61:\\t// the bound sections; DischargedClauses is how many of those a binding\\n62:\\t// enumerates with a verified excerpt and an acceptance owner.\\n70:\\tNormativeClauses    int\\n71:\\tDischargedClauses   int\\n125:\\tClauses         []dischargedClause `json:\\\"clauses,omitempty\\\"`\\n129:// The claim is not taken on trust: the level is recomputed from the clauses the\\n130:// binding enumerates against the clause inventory the pinned specification\\n136:\\t// coverageFull means every normative clause the pinned section carries is\\n137:\\t// enumerated with a verified excerpt and an acceptance owner.\\n144:\\t// coverageUnevidenced means the binding enumerates no clause at all. It says\\n145:\\t// the registry makes no clause-level claim, not that the implementation\\n148:\\t// coverageUnmeasured means normativeKeywordPattern finds no clause line\\n165:// dischargedClause binds one normative clause of the pinned section to the\\n167:// hash-verified document: the identifier must index the section's own clause\\n168:// inventory, the line must be the line that clause occupies, and the excerpt\\n169:// must be that clause's text quoted verbatim, so a clause cannot be claimed\\n171:type dischargedClause struct {\\n174:\\tExcerpt         string   `json:\\\"excerpt\\\"`\\n178:// normativeClause is one RFC 2119 clause line of the pinned specification,\\n180:type normativeClause struct {\\n304:\\t\\t\\t\\\"verified normative lock document digest %s differs from the pinned clause source %s\\\",\\n426:\\t\\t\\t// gate exists to refuse. Absence of a scanner-visible clause is a\\n431:\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\\"assigned section %q binding %q discharges %s normative clauses, which is %s coverage; assigned-scope admission requires full: %s\\\",\\n464:\\t\\treport.NormativeClauses += measured.Total\\n465:\\t\\treport.DischargedClauses += measured.Discharged\\n494:\\t\\t\\tif group.Coverage != \\\"\\\" || group.Gap != \\\"\\\" || len(group.Clauses) != 0 {\\n994:// specification line a clause an implementation has to discharge. MAY and\\n999:// clauseIdentifierPattern matches the \\\"<section>#<index>\\\" form of a clause id.\\n1000:var clauseIdentifierPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^(.+)#([1-9][0-9]*)$`)\\n1074:// sectionClauseInventory measures every normative clause the pinned document\\n1078:func sectionClauseInventory(document *specdoc.Document, key string) ([]normativeClause, error) {\\n1084:\\tvar result []normativeClause\\n1097:\\t\\tresult = append(result, normativeClause{\\n1143:// enumerated clause is a real obligation of the claimed section, quoted\\n1146:// cannot decide that the named acceptance case exercises the clause's meaning —\\n1154:\\tinventory, err := sectionClauseInventory(document, key)\\n1156:\\t\\treturn sectionCoverage{}, fail(\\\"section binding %q clause inventory: %v\\\", key, err)\\n1158:\\tbyIdentifier := make(map[string]normativeClause, len(inventory))\\n1159:\\tfor _, clause := range inventory {\\n1160:\\t\\tbyIdentifier[clause.ID] = clause\\n1167:\\tseen := make(map[string]struct{}, len(group.Clauses))\\n1168:\\tfor _, declared := range group.Clauses {\\n1169:\\t\\tclause, known := byIdentifier[declared.ID]\\n1172:\\t\\t\\t\\t\\\"section binding %q discharges clause %q, which is not one of the %d normative clauses of the pinned section\\\",\\n1176:\\t\\t\\treturn sectionCoverage{}, fail(\\\"section binding %q repeats discharged clause %q\\\", key, declared.ID)\\n1179:\\t\\tif declared.Line != clause.Line {\\n1181:\\t\\t\\t\\t\\\"section binding %q clause %q declares line %d, but the pinned clause is at line %d\\\",\\n1182:\\t\\t\\t\\tkey, declared.ID, declared.Line, clause.Line)\\n===\\n    1316 internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3596,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 899,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
