ory.roots namespace/cardinality (6/7/8/8 across RPC 2/3/4/5) and matches roots to requested namespaces, and hostchannel dispatches authorized post-hello inventory.roots calls through the current-generation gate (TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel). No Merkle digest verification, schema membership or object exchange exists. No clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\nexit status 1\\n--- section 17.1:\\nspec-to-code traceability check failed: assigned section \\\"17.1\\\" binding \\\"section:17.1\\\" discharges 3/6 normative clauses, which is partial coverage; assigned-scope admission requires full: Section 17.1 clauses 17.1#2 (minor-version semantic preservation) and 17.1#6 (v1 materialization upgrade) are outside Negotiate, which selects majors only: no minor-selection entry exists, immutable-object namespaced extensions (17.1#3) belong to the object-exchange owners, and materialization upgrade belongs to the matjournal and provhost owners. The retained config-versioned-readers case keeps the config Decode lanes traceable.\\nexit status 1\\n--- section 17.4:\\nspec-to-code traceability check failed: assigned section \\\"17.4\\\" binding \\\"section:17.4\\\" discharges 1/4 normative clauses, which is sliver coverage; assigned-scope admission requires full: Section 17.4 clauses 17.4#1 through 17.4#3 (upgrade checks, downgraded-binary read-only mode, no resume or transfer) are outside Negotiate: no upgrade, downgrade, or auto-resume flow exists in the tree, so only the activation-unavailable exposure clause discharges above. The retained config cases keep the AssessCompatibility downgrade-assessment lanes traceable.\\nexit status 1\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2588,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 647,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
