or the two parsed bodies (`hello`, `inventory.roots`) with pinned\n22|   sentinels; bound witnesses (nonce 16B admit/15B refuse, standard-alphabet\n23|   and padded refusals, contracts 16/17, line/object floors and their\n24|   independence); per-member namespace vocabulary incl. near-miss and\n25|   future-major refusals; 30-cell namespace mismatch matrix; unknown-field\n26|   sweep over every closed shape; both §17.1 extension directions; response\n27|   correlation classes; major-1 rejection at every entry; error-schema\n28|   negotiation refusal; framing bounds with literal byte counts.\n29|2. `internal/rpcwire/fuzz_adversarial_test.go` (new, 3 targets):\n30|   `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` (24-op vocabulary + adversarial names, admits\n31|   round-trip and never reinterpret), `FuzzNamespaceVocabulary` (oracle\n32|   transcribed from the spec text, not derived from production),\n33|   `FuzzUnknownFields` (admitted lines carry exactly the closed member sets).\n34|   Seeded corpora, deterministic, no network, `-parallel=1`.\n35|3. `internal/meshneg/adversarial_test.go` (new, 4 tests) + one N3 row in\n36|   `negotiate_test.go`: per-key membership sweep (every frame × every profile\n37|   key, missing + substituted, through `Negotiate`), Local-fact pins on shape\n38|   and mixed refusals, six no-coercion shapes and major-1 lanes through the\n39|   composed entry.\n40|4. `internal/matjournal/rpc_replay_test.go` (new, 1 test): lost-response\n41|   recovery through the adopted journal owner — committed phase learned via\n42|   `Get`, blind retry replays byte-identical bytes with a single journal.\n43|5. Harnesses: +6 meshneg probes (37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text\n44|   SURVIVED, exit 0), +7 rpcwire probes (40 killed / neutral passed / new\n45|   `error-text` SURVIVED control, exit 0). One rpcwire row is an honest\n46|   sentinel-swap (`correlation-id-maps-frame`), labeled as swap, not narrowing;\n47|   one is a token-preserving narrowing (`namespace-admits-six