xact member set` |\n81|| FuzzNamespaceVocabulary | inventory admits `credential` | FAIL exit 1: `invalid 3.0.0 namespaces admitted: {\"namespaces\":[\"credential\"]}` |\n82|| FuzzUnknownFields | envelope admits one `extra=true` member | FAIL exit 1: `admitted envelope carries 6 members, want exactly 5` |\n83|\n84|Notes: the first bodies smoke reported a \"finding\" that was an oracle bug\n85|(JSON replaces invalid UTF-8 in operation names; guarded with\n86|`utf8.ValidString`, corpus file removed). Controls must use `-fuzztime=100x`:\n87|`10x` caps TOTAL execs including seeds, so late seeds never run (the bodies\n88|control falsely passed at 10x and fails at 100x).\n89|\n90|## Digest derivation (gate-computed, not copied)\n91|\n92|Command and output after editing the registry, before re-pinning:\n93|\n94|```text\n95|$ go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n96|spec-to-code traceability check failed: ownership registry projection digest 1500e2590662030e66cdd4831aa03cd58827aa292f8b11fa7ec25ecf6d40ad0a differs from reviewed d3eca9063c0f7b7a6abc38a7f53c5d6c01bdbc076886e19a2c66e0a87693e58a\n97|```\n98|\n99|`reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in `internal/traceability/traceability.go`\n100|was set to `1500e259…f6d40ad0a`. Full `tracecheck` is green:\n101|\n102|```text\n103|traceability ok: contracts=63 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=138 fixtures=32 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0\n104|section coverage: bindings=65 full=2 partial=8 sliver=6 unevidenced=45 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=57/535\n105|```\n106|\n107|Section-scoped runs refuse admission (the gate requires `full`), quoting the\n108|measured ratios verbatim:\n109|\n110|- `--section 11.2`: `discharges 3/5 normative clauses, which is partial coverage`\n111|- `--section 11.3`: `discharges 1/27 normative clauses, which is sliver coverage`\n112|- `--section 17.1`: `discharges 3/6 normative clauses, which is partial coverage`\n113|- `--section 17.4`: `discharges 1/4 normative clauses, which is sliver coverage`\n114|\n115|(Full refusal texts with gaps: `evidence/tracecheck-section-*.log`.)\n116|\n117|## Inherited advisories N1-N3 (all closed)\n118|\n119|- N1: sweep kills per-key exemption plants at every key (reviewer's S7/S8/S9\n120|  class); missing-key cases pin the length arm, substituted-key cases pin the\n121|  membership loop (the distinction is load-bearing: S6-style count plants stay\n122|  subsumed).\n123|- N2: `refusal.Local == LocalMajors(generation)` asserted on all 176\n124|  shape/mixed sweep rows plus 5 dedicated mixed rows; kills S12.\n125|- N3: `refuse-local-names-1` row placed beside a common major `([1,2]` vs\n126|  `[2]`) after the first revision (`[1]` vs `[2]`) proved unobservable — the\n127|  disjoint refusal subsumes the plant. The harness caught it (SURVIVED),\n128|  fixed before the evidence run. Reachability bound stated: `LocalMajors`\n129|  never yields 1, so only a direct `Select` caller observes the arm.\n130|\n131|## Validation (all run by the producer in this session)\n132|\n133|| # | Command | Exit |\n134|| --- | --- | --- |\n135|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l …)\"` | 0 |\n136|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n137|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n138|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1` | 0, 38 ok |\n139|| 5 | `go test … -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` in 5 chunks (sessquery alone: 345s) | 0, 38 ok, no DATA RACE |\n140|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0, 38 ok |\n141|| 7-23 | 17 fuzz smokes incl. the 3 new targets | all 0 |\n142|| 24 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (57/535) |\n143|| 25 | `cataloggen -adopted … -check` | 0, tree unchanged |\n144|| 26-27 | `GOOS=linux/windows go build ./...` | 0 / 0 |\n145|| 28 | JSON census over tracked `*.json` | 0 |\n146|| 29 | `task-board validate` | 0 (185 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY warnings only) |\n147|| 30 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n148|\n149|Package coverage: meshneg 87.8%, rpcwire 99.1%. Mutants: see §5 above;\n150|per-plant raw logs + `results.json` + `table.md` in the evidence tar.\n151|Nothing was accepted from prior evidence except the trunk baseline all runs\n152|started from; every row above was executed in this session.\n153|\n154|## Incidents (no evidence depends on them)\n155|\n156|1. A shell `>` typo in an early survey grep truncated\n157|   `internal/matjournal/journal_test.go`; restored byte-identical from the\n158|   checkpoint (`git checkout --`, clean status verified). The matjournal test\n159|   inventory used afterwards was re-taken from the restored file.\n160|2. A `testdata/fuzz` cleanup pass deleted tracked corpus files under\n161|   `internal/canonicaljson` and `internal/scalar`; restored byte-identical\n162|   from the checkpoint the same way. Final `git status` shows only the 15\n163|   candidate paths below.\n164|\n165|## Candidate file inventory (`git status`)\n166|\n167|Modified (11): LOGBOOK.md, README.md, internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md,\n168|internal/meshneg/mutations.py, internal/meshneg/negotiate_test.go,\n169|internal/rpcwire/mutations.py, internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go,\n170|internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json, internal/traceability/traceability.go,\n171|internal/traceability/traceability_test.go, task-board.config.json.\n172|New (4): internal/matjournal/rpc_replay_test.go,\n173|internal/meshneg/adversarial_test.go, internal/rpcwire/adversarial_test.go,\n174|internal/rpcwire/fuzz_adversarial_test.go.\n175|\n176|## Stated bounds (summary; owners in the matrix)\n177|\n178|22/24 §11.3 operation bodies opaque (no initiator/lease parser or\n179|pre-mutation revalidation entry); lease/materialization embedded-type\n180|vocabularies unwitnessed at RPC; no minor-selection entry; envelope\n181|`request_id` correlation-only (no responder replay cache); chunk-data\n182|base64url unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC/meshneg\n183|purity (no durable writes — crash/idempotency evidence adopted from the\n184|matjournal suite). 17.2/17.3 registry bindings keep their existing\n185|unevidenced owners.","final_result":true}}}
