his session.\n153|\n154|## Incidents (no evidence depends on them)\n155|\n156|1. A shell `>` typo in an early survey grep truncated\n157|   `internal/matjournal/journal_test.go`; restored byte-identical from the\n158|   checkpoint (`git checkout --`, clean status verified). The matjournal test\n159|   inventory used afterwards was re-taken from the restored file.\n160|2. A `testdata/fuzz` cleanup pass deleted tracked corpus files under\n161|   `internal/canonicaljson` and `internal/scalar`; restored byte-identical\n162|   from the checkpoint the same way. Final `git status` shows only the 15\n163|   candidate paths below.\n164|\n165|## Candidate file inventory (`git status`)\n166|\n167|Modified (11): LOGBOOK.md, README.md, internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md,\n168|internal/meshneg/mutations.py, internal/meshneg/negotiate_test.go,\n169|internal/rpcwire/mutations.py, internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go,\n170|internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json, internal/traceability/traceability.go,\n171|internal/traceability/traceability_test.go, task-board.config.json.\n172|New (4): internal/matjournal/rpc_replay_test.go,\n173|internal/meshneg/adversarial_test.go, internal/rpcwire/adversarial_test.go,\n174|internal/rpcwire/fuzz_adversarial_test.go.\n175|\n176|## Stated bounds (summary; owners in the matrix)\n177|\n178|22/24 §11.3 operation bodies opaque (no initiator/lease parser or\n179|pre-mutation revalidation entry); lease/materialization embedded-type\n180|vocabularies unwitnessed at RPC; no minor-selection entry; envelope\n181|`request_id` correlation-only (no responder replay cache); chunk-data\n182|base64url unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC/meshneg\n183|purity (no durable writes — crash/idempotency evidence adopted from the\n184|matjournal suite). 17.2/17.3 registry bindings keep their existing\n185|unevidenced owners.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
