gest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\n+- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\"x\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\n+- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\n+- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"LOGBOOK.md","added":13,"removed":3},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
